title: 'Perl on Windows: a dead lock owner is only broken after the stale age'
updated: 2026-11-14T00:42:50Z
---

From k186. Skilletor::State::_dead_owner decides a lock owner is gone when kill 0 fails with ESRCH; on Windows perl returns EINVAL for a pid that no longer exists, so a lock a crashed run left is broken only after stale_ms (300 s) instead of at once. Treat EINVAL as gone on MSWin32 (check what node does in the reference: process.kill(pid, 0) throws ESRCH there), with a test through the injected win32 seam.
